sandbox (2.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * add --uid: run the command under a UID and GID of 2000000000-2000999999
    that has no passwd, group, subuid or subgid entry; refused for a root
    caller, and the IDs are checked after the drop
  * add --cpu_max: write cpu.max of the cgroup
  * add --tmp_size: mount a nosuid,nodev tmpfs of the given size at /tmp
  * add --stop_fifo and --stop_grace: on a byte from the caller's FIFO, or
    SIGTERM/SIGINT to the tool, send SIGTERM and SIGKILL after the grace
  * add --version
  * build the sandbox tree through file descriptors; refuse sandbox parents
    not owned by the caller, other than a shared sticky folder such as /tmp
  * follow no link in the tree and enter no mount when removing it; put files
    in before mounts, refuse a mount under another mount, copy files without
    set-ID bits, and run ldd as the caller
  * a SIGTERM or SIGINT during setup now kills the child as soon as it
    starts; the tool still exits 1
  * refuse a stop FIFO that its group or others may read
  * make the on-disk /tmp sticky (1777); copy, not link, someone else's
    set-ID file for a non-root caller; remove a tree of any depth, with the
    mounts in it, without recursion
  * delete a cgroup only when it is empty, never moving processes out of it
  * refuse an existing cgroup unless it is an empty leaf and, for a non-root
    caller, one the tool made for that caller
  * claim a new cgroup with mkdir before writing into it, so two runs naming
    it at once cannot share it

 -- Sergey Svistunov <sergey-svistunov@yandex.ru>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0000

