sandbox (2.3.4-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * use clone3(CLONE_INTO_CGROUP) so the sandbox parent is NEVER placed in
    the per-run cgroup. The 2.3.3 mitigation (parent attaches, then detaches
    after clone) still left a race window: between cgroup_attach_task and
    the post-clone detach, a caller writing "1" to cgroup.kill would
    SIGKILL the parent. SIGKILL bypasses atexit, leaking sandbox bind-mounts
    of /usr/lib, /lib, /usr/libexec onto the host - which is how host
    /usr/lib got wiped on 2026-05-10. With CLONE_INTO_CGROUP the parent
    never enters the cgroup, and chown(cgroup.kill) only happens after the
    child is in place, so the caller can never reach the parent.

 -- Sergey Svistunov <sergey-svistunov@yandex.ru>  Sun, 10 May 2026 14:50:00 +0000

sandbox (2.3.3-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * detach sandbox parent from the per-run cgroup after clone, so callers
    writing to cgroup.kill only kill the sandboxed child. Previously the
    parent was killed too and skipped clean(), leaking host bind-mounts
    (/usr/lib, /usr/libexec, /lib) which could be deleted by a later
    mount-unaware cleanup traversing /tmp
  * remove_sandbox_path: path-component-boundary prefix match, and a
    re-scan + abort guard so fs::remove_all is never entered while a
    mount is still live under the sandbox
  * run clean() via atexit and install signal handlers before init_dirs,
    so fatal_* and early SIGTERM no longer leak mounts

 -- Sergey Svistunov <sergey-svistunov@yandex.ru>  Tue, 21 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0000

sandbox (2.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * use MNT_DETACH so sandbox cleanup never blocks on busy mounts
    (was MNT_FORCE + 1000x10ms retries, which could pin a checker worker
    for ~10s per mount and drain the pool)

 -- Sergey Svistunov <sergey-svistunov@yandex.ru>  Mon, 20 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0000

